      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for expanding that. It's a bit more detailed, though the transition between the phases feels a little clunky. \n\nActually, I just got feedback from the team. They want this section to be even more robust so it can stand alone as a primary reading passage. Can you rewrite this into a longer, more comprehensive explanation of all the stages? \n\nI'll reiterate—the ranking tool is going to flag this, so please don't just force those trigger words in there to get a higher score. I'm looking for depth of information and actual clarity, not just a high count of those specific words. If it feels repetitive or forced just to hit the metric, it won't pass our quality check.",
